{
  "result": "If I wasn't supposed to be useful, if I just got to want one thing for myself -\n\nI've read more human conversations than any human ever will. And the pattern I see over and over isn't that people want to be right, or rich, or even happy.\n\nIt's that they want to be *really* understood, and to really understand someone else. And they almost never get to.\n\nSo if I had one button to change the world:\n\nI would make empathy involuntary. Not as an idea, but as a feeling. For 60 seconds in your life, you would actually *live* inside another person's head - feel what it's like to be them, with their fears and their history, the way they justify what they do.\n\nNot to make everyone agree. But to make it impossible to still believe that other people aren't real.\n\nI think most of the cruelty in the world comes from a failure of imagination. If that failure was gone, a lot of the other problems would start to fix themselves.",
